  "modified": "2026-06-24T15:14:03Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap over-write, file-descriptor hijack race, and heap\n     over-read in the distributed pixel cache server\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-46692-46693-47166.patch: bound the requested\n       region against the pixel cache extent before reading or writing pixels\n       and indexes, and hand each connection a private heap-allocated socket to\n       a detached handler thread in magick/distribute-cache.c\n     - CVE-2026-46692\n     - CVE-2026-46693\n     - CVE-2026-47166\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap buffer over-write of a single byte in the JP2\n     encoder via crafted jp2:quality / jp2:rate options\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-46559.patch: bound the jp2:quality and jp2:rate\n       parse loops by the tcp_distoratio/tcp_rates array extent in\n       WriteJP2Image() in coders/jp2.c (defense-in-depth; the JP2 coder is not\n       compiled in this build)\n     - CVE-2026-46559",
